**Potential coalitions:**
Republican Socialist Conjunction (PSOE + [+ ar_name +] + PRRS + PRR + DLR + Other Left Republicans + Other Right Republicans): [+ republican_socialist_conjunction +]%

Left Republican Coalition (PSOE + [+ ar_name +] + PRRS + Other Left Republicans): [+ left_republican_coalition +]%

Popular Front (PSOE + [+ ar_name +] + PRRS + Other Left Republicans + PCE + Regionalists): [+ popular_front +]%

Right Wing Coalition (PRR + [+ ap_name +] + Agrarians + DLR + Other Right Republicans): [+ right_coalition +]%

Left Front (PSOE + PCE): [+ left_front +]%

[? if ap_r >= 20 : The rapid rise in ap_name votes is extremely worrying. Many had believed that the party was marginal; now, some of us consider it to be the greatest threat to the republic in Spain. ?]

[? if anti_democratic_coalition >= 50 : Together, the anti-democratic PCE, ap_name and jons_name have a majority in the Cortes. A stable governing majority will be almost impossible. ?]

There are some potential coalition arrangements.

@coalition_menu

- @psoe_majority
- @left_republican_coalition
- @republican_socialist_conjuction
- @no_majority
- @left_front
- @popular_front
- @right_coalition
- @far_right_coalition
- @ap_majority

@popular_front
title: Form a Popular Front against the anti-republican right?
subtitle: PSOE + PRRS + Other Left Republicans + [+ ar_name +] [? if ur_formed: + UR ?] [? if poum_formed: + POUM ?]([+ popular_front_coalition +]%)
unavailable-subtitle: PSOE + PRRS + Other Left Republicans + [+ ar_name +] [? if ur_formed: + UR ?] [? if poum_formed: + POUM ?]([+ popular_front_coalition +]%) - [? if (pce_relation < 65): We do not have good enough relations with the PCE. ?][? if (ar_relation < 45 and prrs_relation < 45): We do not have good enough relations with the [+ ar_name +] and the PRRS. ?][? if communist_coalition < 3 : The Communists are unwilling to compromise at all. ?]
view-if: popular_front_coalition >= 50
choose-if: ((pce_relation >= 65) and (ar_relation >= 45 and prrs_relation >= 45))

We could unify all leftist parties to ensure a progressist governement.

The conservatives and some officers won't be happy.

- @popular_front_2: Form the Popular Front!

@popular_front_2
view-if: ((pce_relation < 65) and (ar_relation < 45 and prrs_relation < 45))

Somehow, all the leftist parties, even the CNT, are at the very least willing to entertain negotiations. Of course, PCE and CNT radicals derail the negotiations almost immediately.

- @popular_front_resources
- @popular_front_democracy
- @popular_front_azana
- @coalition_menu: This is impossible. Try another governing arrangement.

@popular_front_resources
title: Use our resources to smooth things over.
unavailable-subtitle: Required: 4 resources
subtitle: -4 resources
choose-if: resources >= 4
on-arrival: resources -= 4
go-to: popular_front_success

@popular_front_democracy
title: Convince the PCE to accept democracy.
subtitle: After the VII Congress of the III International, the leadership of the PCE at least claim to support the Popular Front.
unavailable-subtitle: Our relationship with the PCE is not high enough.
choose-if: (pce_relation >= 60 and communist_coalition >= 3)
go-to: popular_front_success

@popular_front_azana
title: Use pressure from President Azana to force the parties to cooperate.
view-if: president == "Azana"
go-to: popular_front_success

@popular_front_success
on-arrival: psoe_in_government = 1; in_popular_front = 1; chancellor = "Casares Quiroga"; chancellor_party = ar_name; pce_relation += 10; coup_progress += 2; in_left_front = 0; in_republican_socialist_conjunction_coalition = 0; in_left_republican_coalition = 0; in_right_front = 0; coalition_dissent = 0;
go-to: popular_front_civil_war if coup_progress >= 10; popular_front_no_civil_war if coup_progress < 10
achievement: volksfront

Somehow, surprisingly, the coalition is successfully formed! We still need a President of the Council of Ministers; the only acceptable choice among the parties was Casares Quiroga of the [+ ar_name +].

@popular_front_no_civil_war
on-arrival: pce_goals_seen = 0; finance_minister_party = ar_name; interior_minister_party = ar_name; economic_minister_party = "I"; labor_minister_party = ar_name; foreign_minister_party = ar_name; agriculture_minister_party = ar_name; reichswehr_minister = "I"; leverage = psoe_r + pce_r;
achievement: volksfront

In response to the PCE's and CNT's entrance into the government, the right-wing takes a "wait-and-see" approach for now. They expect that the Popular Front government will be unstable and incompetent, and will collapse of its own accord, discrediting the left and center and eventually enabling the destruction of the Spanish Republic. Our task is to prove them wrong.

The PCE and CNT have taken an abstentionist position with regards to ministries. They claim to be participating as the "loyal opposition" within the Popular Front government, supporting us from the outside while also running their own propaganda campaigns to turn workers to their side.

- @ministries: First, we must select our ministries.


@popular_front_civil_war
on-arrival: pce_relation = 80; ejercito_loyalty += 0.25;

In response to the victory of the Popular Front, the right-wing immediately launches a coup attempt. Columns of falangists, carlists and nationalists rose up in different points of Spain. The African Army in Morocco joins the coup. Reactionary officers within the Ejercito have taken their troops out of the barracks and joined them with the reactionary forces to stop us from taking power.

The President manages to diffuse some of the hostility from the Ejercito and the Security Forces, but fail to prevent the outbreak of fighting. We are forced to fight on the same side as the PCE and CNT, whether we want to or not.

- @civil_war: A civil war, then.



@far_right_coalition
title: Far-right coalition
subtitle: PRR + CEDA + Agrarians ([+ far_right_coalition +]%)
view-if: far_right_coalition >= 50
go-to: far_right_win if ((year >= 1934 or ap_r >= 44) and (president != "Prieto" and president != "Largo Caballero")); far_right_fail if (year < 1934 and ap_r < 44); far_right_braun if (president == "Prieto" or president == "Largo Caballero)
priority: 2

There are enough votes for the Radicals and the CEDA to form a coalition alongside the agrarians. It is up to President [+ president +] to decide.

@far_right_win
on-arrival: chancellor = ap_leader; chancellor_party = ap_name

[? if president == "Alcala-Zamora" : President Alcala-Zamora ?][? if president == "Prieto" : President Prieto somehow ?][? if president == "Largo Caballero" : President Largo Caballero somehow ?]  has decided that the [+ ap_name +] and PRR can form governement because it is what the constitution would stipulate.

- @hitler_takes_power: What do we do now?


@far_right_fail
on-arrival: chancellor = "Lerroux"; chancellor_party = "PRR"; pro_republic -= 10; next_election_time = time+5; next_election_month = month + 5; next_election_year = year; next_election_year += 1 if next_election_month > 12; next_election_month -= 12 if next_election_month > 12;

The President is very skeptical of the CEDA because they refuse to oath loyalty to the Constitution and the Republic, so instead, [+ president +] appoints Alejandro Lerroux, leader of the PRR and second force of the parliament to form governement without CEDA ministers.

The CEDA is out of the governement... For the meantime. 

New elections have been set for [+ next_election_month : month +] [+ next_election_year +].

@far_right_braun
on-arrival: coup_progress += 2

President [+ president +] faces a dilemma. Is it "democratic" to let democracy be destroyed, if the majority of voters have willed it so? Some, even on the left, suggest that the CEDA would not *truly* be as horrific as their platform suggests, and that giving them power would let them discredit themselves in the eyes of the public.

Alternatively, [+ president +] could use the emergency powers of the presidency. Articles 42 and 80 could be used to stop an incumbing CEDA governement, it would need the approval of the Cortes. 

- @emergency_braun: We will form an emergency government with [+ president +]'s support.
- @new_elections: We will have new elections.
- @far_right_win: Let the CEDA in the government.


@left_coalition
title: Is a United Left coalition possible?
subtitle: SPD + KPD [? if sapd_formed: + SAPD ?] ([+ left_coalition +]%)
unavailable-subtitle: SPD + KPD [? if sapd_formed: + SAPD ?] ([+ left_coalition +]%). [? if kpd_relation < 50 : We do not have adequate relations with the KPD. ?][? if communist_coalition < 3 : The Communists are too committed to their radical ways to partake in government. ?]
view-if: left_coalition >= 50
choose-if: (kpd_relation >= 50 or (kpd_party_leader == "Conciliators" and kpd_relation >= 40)) and communist_coalition >= 3

There are enough votes for a SPD + KPD coalition government, if such a thing were actually possible.

The far-right might attempt a coup, if such a coalition were formed.

- @left_coalition_impossible: This is impossible.
- @left_coalition_possible: This could be possible.

@left_coalition_impossible
go-to: coalition_menu

A far left coalition is impossible.


@left_coalition_possible

The KPD is still very reluctant to join a coalition, despite grassroots friendliness between our memberships. The Stalinist leadership is vehemently against such a thing. They demand the appointment of Ernst Thälmann as chancellor in exchange for a coalition. [? if president == "Hindenburg" : There is no chance whatsoever that President Hindenburg would approve of the appointment of a die-hard communist as chancellor. ?] Alternatively, if our relations with them are good enough, we could convince them to support the appointment of one of our centrist or left-leaning members as chancellor.

- @thalmann_chancellor: Appoint Thälmann as chancellor.
- @left_coalition_resources
- @left_coalition_relations
- @coalition_menu: Try a different governing arrangement.

@thalmann_chancellor
choose-if: president == "Braun" and reformist_strength + neorevisionist_strength < left_strength
unavailable-subtitle: [? if president != "Braun": President [+ president +] would never allow such a thing. ?] [? if reformist_strength >= left_strength : Most in the parliamentary party would not support Thälmann as chancellor. ?]
on-arrival: chancellor = "Thälmann"; chancellor_party = "KPD"; kpd_relation = 80; in_left_front = 1; spd_in_government = 1 

With great reluctance, President [+ president +] appoints [+ chancellor +] as chancellor.

Immediately, [+ chancellor +] goes to work building a "Soviet Germany": consolidating as much power as possible in the KPD, purging state institutions of anti-communists, and sending street fighters against the "enemies of the people".

In response to [+ chancellor +] being appointed Chancellor, the right-wing forces launches almost immediately launch an attempted coup. Troops of the Stahlhelm and Nazi SA enter Berlin and immediately begin clashing with our supporters! Reactionary officers within the Reichswehr have taken their troops out of the barracks and joined them with the Stahlhelm to stop the KPD from taking power. We are forced to be on the same side as the KPD, whether we want to or not.

- @civil_war


@left_coalition_resources
title: Use our resources to smooth things over.
unavailable-subtitle: Required: 3 resources
subtitle: -3 resources
choose-if: resources >= 3
on-arrival: resources -= 3
go-to: left_coalition_success

@left_coalition_relations
title: Convince the KPD to accept democracy.
unavailable-subtitle: Our relationships with the KPD are not good enough.
choose-if: kpd_relation >= 60 or kpd_party_leader == "Conciliators"
go-to: left_coalition_success


@left_coalition_success
on-arrival: spd_in_government = 1; in_left_front = 1; chancellor = "Breitscheid"; chancellor_party = "SPD"; coup_progress += 3; capital_strike_progress += 2; in_popular_front = 0; in_grand_coalition = 0; in_weimar_coalition = 0; kpd_relation += 10
go-to: left_coalition_civil_war if coup_progress >= 10; left_coalition_no_civil_war if coup_progress < 10
achievement: einheitsfront

Somehow, surprisingly, the left coalition is successfully formed, without appointing Thälmann as chancellor. The consensus choice for chancellor, accepted by the SPD, KPD, and President [+ president +], is Rudolf Breitscheid, who belongs to the centrist faction of the SPD, but was acceptable to the left due to his previous membership in the left-wing anti-war USPD.

# just raise the coup limit, don't immediately go to civil war

@left_coalition_no_civil_war
on-arrival: kpd_goals_seen = 0; foreign_minister_party = "SPD"; interior_minister_party = "SPD"; justice_minister_party = "SPD"; labor_minister_party = "SPD"; reichswehr_minister_party = "SPD"; economic_minister_party = "SPD"; finance_minister_party = "SPD"; agriculture_minister_party = "SPD"; reichswehr_loyalty -= 0.05

In response to the KPD's entrance into the government, the right-wing takes a "wait-and-see" approach for now. They expect that our government will be unstable and incompetent, and will collapse of its own accord, discrediting the left and eventually enabling the destruction of the Weimar Republic. Our task is to prove them wrong.

The KPD has taken an abstentionist position with regards to ministries. They claim to be participating as the "loyal opposition" in the worker's government, supporting us from the outside while also running their own propaganda campaigns to turn workers to their side. They seem to expect that we would inevitably fail, and that our failure would benefit them. 

Whatever their reasoning is, the SPD has control over the ministries of government.

@left_coalition_civil_war
on-arrival: reichswehr_loyalty += 0.1

In response to the KPD's entrance into the government, the right-wing immediately launches a coup attempt. Troops of the Stahlhelm and Nazi SA enter Berlin and begin clashing with our supporters. Reactionary officers within the Reichswehr have taken their troops out of the barracks and joined them with the Stahlhelm to stop us from taking power.

- @civil_war: A civil war, then.



@right_coalition
title: Refuse to form a government, so that a right-wing coalition may be formed.
subtitle: Z + BVP + DVP + DNVP + Others ([+ right_coalition +]%)
unavailable-subtitle: The DNVP is not interested in a coalition with the Center.
view-if: right_coalition >= 50
choose-if: year < 1929

There are enough votes for a right-wing coalition of the Center (+ BVP), DVP, DNVP, and minor conservative parties. [? if largest_party == "SPD": However, this will be seen as abdicating responsibility for government, as we are the largest party. ?]

- @right_coalition_sure: Yes, we will abdicate our responsibility for government formation, and let a right-wing coalition take power.
- @grand_coalition: Actually, we wish to form a grand coalition after all.

@no_right_coalition
go-to: no_majority

However, the DNVP and its leader Hugenberg is refusing to partake in a coalition with the "November criminals" in the Center Party. Thus, there is no clear path towards a Reichstag majority.

@right_coalition_sure
subtitle: This will be extremely unpopular within our party.
on-arrival: pro_republic -= 5; center_dissent += 15; left_dissent += 10; labor_dissent += 25; reformist_dissent += 25; neorevisionist_dissent += 15; z_relation -= 5; ddp_relation -= 5; dvp_relation -= 5
go-to: right_coalition_2


@right_coalition_2
unavailable-subtitle: The DNVP is not interested in a coalition with the Center.
view-if: right_coalition >= 50
choose-if: year < 1929
on-arrival: spd_in_government = 0; spd_toleration = 0; chancellor = "Brüning"; chancellor_party = "Z"; foreign_minister_party = "DVP"; interior_minister_party = "DNVP"; justice_minister_party = "DNVP"; labor_minister_party = "Z"; reichswehr_minister_party = "I"; economic_minister_party = "DVP"; finance_minister_party = "Z"; agriculture_minister_party = "DNVP"; in_right_coalition = 1;

Even though the DNVP is very reluctant to participate in such a coalition, they still accede to President Hindenburg's wishes. Thus, a majority center-right coalition is formed, with Brüning as chancellor.



@no_majority
title: There is no clear governing majority.
view-if: left_republican_coalition < 50 and left_front < 50 and popular_front < 50 and right_coalition < 50 and (republican_socialist_conjuction < 50 or (year >= 1932 and prr_leader == "Lerroux")) and president = "Alcala-Zamora" and far_right_coalition < 50
on-arrival: no_majority_elections += 1
go-to: no_majority_bruning if chancellor = "Lerroux" or chancellor = "Martinez Barrio" or chancellor = "Samper"; no_majority_papen if chancellor = "Portela" and no_majority_papen_elections == 0; no_majority_papen_2 if chancellor == "Portela" and no_majority_papen_elections > 0; no_majority_schleicher if chancellor = "Schleicher"; no_majority_spd if chancellor_party = "PSOE" or chancellor == "Azana"

@no_majority_spd
on-arrival: chancellor = "Lerroux"; chancellor_party = "PRR"

There is no path to an obviously workable majority. Since President Alcala-Zamora is unwilling to work with a minority or caretaker PSOE government, his preferred chancellor is Alejandro Lerroux of the Radical Republican Party, who could lead a "presidential" government.

- @toleration_bruning: We will tolerate Lerroux.
- @new_elections: We will have new elections.

@no_majority_bruning
go-to: no_majority_bruning_toleration if (no_majority_elections <= 3 and anti_democratic_coalition <= 50); hindenburg_appoints_papen if no_majority_elections > 3 or anti_democratic_coalition > 50


@hindenburg_appoints_papen
on-arrival: chancellor = "Chapaprieta"; chancellor_party = "I"; next_election_time = time+3; next_election_month = month + 3; next_election_year = year; next_election_year += 1 if next_election_month > 12; next_election_month -= 12 if next_election_month > 12; pro_republic -= 8; finance_minister_party = "I"; interior_minister_party = "I"; economic_minister_party = "I"; labor_minister_party = "I"; foreign_minister_party = "I"; agriculture_minister_party = "I"; reichswehr_minister_party = "I"; public_instruction_minister_party = "I"; public_works_minister_party = "I";

There is no path to a majority government. President Alcala-Zamora is tired of the corruption, and appoints Joaquin Chapaprieta y Torregrosa as chancellor instead of a member of the PRR. Chapaprieta is an indenpendent formerly from the Republican Liberal Right Party and Hacienda Minister under Lerroux governement, and looks to create a concentration governement alongside the Republican Radicals, CEDA, agrarians and various right republican parties.

Chapaprieta is immediately faced with a vote of no confidence, given his unpopularity. However the SPD votes, he is guaranteed to fall, due to the unanimous hatred against him from all other parties.

New elections have been set for [+ next_election_month : month +] [+ next_election_year +].

@no_majority_bruning_toleration
on-arrival: no_majority_bruning_elections += 1

There is no path to a majority government. One option would be to have a continuation of the current Radical government; if we tolerate it, then it would retain a majority vote against no-confidence.

Alternatively, we could have new elections.

- @toleration_bruning: We will tolerate Brüning.
- @new_elections: We will have new elections.

@no_majority_papen
on-arrival: pro_republic -= 10; next_election_time = time+3; next_election_month = month + 3; next_election_year = year; next_election_year += 1 if next_election_month > 12; next_election_month -= 12 if next_election_month > 12; workers_nsdap += 6; unemployed_nsdap += 6; old_middle_nsdap += 5; new_middle_nsdap += 5; rural_nsdap += 5; no_majority_papen_elections += 1; workers_spd -= 8 if pro_republic < 45; workers_spd *= 0.85 if pro_republic < 40; workers_nsdap += 5 if pro_republic < 40;

After the elections, Chapaprieta is still deeply unpopular, without any hint of coalition support, and there is a vote of no confidence called against him almost immediately. No matter how we vote, the measure would pass. The Reichstag is dissolved once more.

New elections have been set for [+ next_election_month : month +] [+ next_election_year +].


@no_majority_papen_2
on-arrival: chancellor = "Portela"; pro_republic -= 10; next_election_time = time+5; next_election_month = month + 5; next_election_year = year; next_election_year += 1 if next_election_month > 12; next_election_month -= 12 if next_election_month > 12; workers_nsdap += 5; unemployed_nsdap += 10; old_middle_nsdap += 5; new_middle_nsdap += 5; rural_nsdap += 10; workers_spd -= 8 if pro_republic < 45; workers_spd *= 0.85 if pro_republic < 40; workers_nsdap += 5 if pro_republic < 40; finance_minister_party = "I"; interior_minister_party = "I"; economic_minister_party = "I"; labor_minister_party = "I"; foreign_minister_party = "I"; agriculture_minister_party = "I"; reichswehr_minister = "I";

Chapaprieta fails to implement his reforms due to the opposition of the CEDA. Alcala-Zamora is displeased with Chapaprieta, and calls on him to resign. Now, indenpendent formerly from the Dynastic Liberal Party, Manuel Portela Valladares has been appointed chancellor, again as part of a presidential government.

Portela's government is deeply unpopular among all parties of the Cortes. Despite his support for a centrist build-up, both the left and the right wants new elections.

New elections have been set for [+ next_election_month : month +] [+ next_election_year +].


@no_majority_schleicher
go-to: hitler_chancellor

# TODO: there should be a second Schleicher option if the NSDAP isn't the strongest


@hitler_chancellor
on-arrival: chancellor = "Hitler"; chancellor_party = "NSDAP"

There is no path to a majority government for now. The scheming around President Hindenburg is leading to only one path - that of Chancellor Adolf Hitler. [? if largest_party == "NSDAP" : Since they are the largest party, it is not exactly contrary to parliamentary procedure, so it is difficult to raise objections solely on procedural grounds. ?] [? if hitler_deported: Despite his earlier deportation, the Nazi leaders and their reactionary allies have connived for the president to give him German citizenship after all. ?]

- @hitler_takes_power: What now?

# if NSDAP is largest party and Hindenburg is president, then Hindenburg appoints Hitler chancellor.

@psoe_majority
title: PSOE majority alone CAMBIAR NOMBRE DE MINISTROS
subtitle: PSOE: [+ psoe_r +]%
view-if: psoe_r >= 50
on-arrival: chancellor = "Empty"; chancellor_party = "PSOE"; psoe_in_government = 1; in_psoe_majority = 1; pro_republic += 5; foreign_minister_party = "PSOE"; foreign_minister = "Breitscheid"; interior_minister_party = "PSOE"; interior_minister = "Severing"; justice_minister_party = "PSOE"; justice_minister = "Radbruch"; labor_minister_party = "PSOE"; labor_minister = "Wissell"; reichswehr_minister_party = "PSOE"; reichswehr_minister = "Leber"; economic_minister_party = "PSOE"; economic_minister = "Schmidt"; finance_minister_party = "PSOE"; finance_minister = "Hilferding"; agriculture_minister_party = "PSOE"; agriculture_minister = "Baade"; public_instruction_minister_party = "PSOE"; public_instruction_minister = "Fernando de los Ríos"; public_works_minister_party = "PSOE"; public_works_minister = "Indalecio Prieto"; ejercito_loyalty -= 0.05; 
achievement: majority_party

Finally, the PSOE can govern alone! Our long campaign of electioneering has paid off. We do not need to worry about coalition government; anything is possible. 

Who should be chancellor?

- @prieto_majority_chancellor: Otto Braun for Chancellor.
- @largo_caballero_majority_chancellor: Rudolf Breitscheid for Chancellor.
- @besteiro_majority_chancellor: Hermann Müller for Chancellor.

@prieto_majority_chancellor
view-if: not historical_mode or not spd_prussia
on-arrival: chancellor = "Prieto"

[? if president == "Braun": Our experts have checked the constitution, and have discovered that there is no specific prohibition against the Chancellor also being the President (the President may not be a member of the Reichstag; there is no law saying that the Chancellor must be a member of the Reichstag). Thus, we have Chancellor-President Otto Braun. ?]
[? if president != "Braun": Indalecio Prieto has become President of the Council of Ministers of the PSOE majority. ?]

@largo_caballero_majority_chancellor
on-arrival: chancellor = "Largo Caballero"

Francisco Largo Caballero has become President of the Council of Ministers of the PSOE majority.

@besteiro_majority_chancellor
view-if: muller_dead = 0
on-arrival: chancellor = "Besteiro"

Julian Besteiro has become President of the Council of Ministers of the PSOE majority.








@brauns_dilemma
title: There is no clear governing majority.
subtitle: President Braun faces a dilemma.
view-if: president == "Braun" and (grand_coalition < 50 or grand_coalition_failed == 1)

President Braun faces a dilemma. He desperately desires a socialist or at least democratic government, but the electoral results are not there for such. Article 48 has been used by Hindenburg to promulgate anti-democratic and anti-worker policies; can Article 48 be used for good as well as evil?

- @emergency_braun: We will form an emergency government with Braun's support.
- @new_elections: We will have new elections.
- @new_grand_coalition
- @left_coalition
- @popular_front_coalition
- @far_right_coalition



@emergency_braun
title: We will form an emergency government with Braun's support.
subtitle: This may have the effect of inflamming public sentiment against us, and the reactionaries will be against us each step of the way.
on-arrival: sa_strength += 100; sh_strength += 100; in_emergency_government = 1

Yes, an emergency minority government, with the support of the SPD. Who should lead this emergency minority government?

- @braun_emergency_chancellor: Francisco Largo Caballero for president of the Council of Ministers.
- @breitscheid_emergency_chancellor: Indalecio Prieto for president of the Council of Ministers.
- @bruning_emergency_chancellor: Martinez Barrios of the Union Republicana, as a goodwill gesture toward the bourgeoisie.
- @wirth_emergency_chancellor: Azana of the Izquierda Republicana, as a gesture of republican unity.

@braun_emergency_chancellor
subtitle: This is unprecedented.
view-if: president != "Largo Caballero"
on-arrival: chancellor = "Largo Caballero"; chancellor_party = "PSOE"; psoe_in_government = 1; in_psoe_majority = 1; pro_republic += 5; foreign_minister_party = "PSOE"; foreign_minister = "Breitscheid"; interior_minister_party = "PSOE"; interior_minister = "Severing"; justice_minister_party = "PSOE"; justice_minister = "Radbruch"; labor_minister_party = "PSOE"; labor_minister = "Wissell"; reichswehr_minister_party = "PSOE"; reichswehr_minister = "Leber"; economic_minister_party = "PSOE"; economic_minister = "Schmidt"; finance_minister_party = "PSOE"; finance_minister = "Hilferding"; agriculture_minister_party = "PSOE"; agriculture_minister = "Baade"; public_instruction_minister_party = "PSOE"; public_instruction_minister = "Fernando de los Ríos"; public_works_minister_party = "PSOE"; public_works_minister = "Indalecio Prieto"; ejercito_loyalty -= 0.1; 

We have appointed Largo Caballero as president of the Council of Ministers.

- @far_right_coup
- @emergency_no_confidence: The Nazis immediately call a no-confidence vote against us...

@breitscheid_emergency_chancellor
view-if: president != "Prieto"
on-arrival: chancellor = "Prieto"; chancellor_party = "PSOE"; psoe_in_government = 1; in_psoe_majority = 1; pro_republic += 5; foreign_minister_party = "PSOE"; foreign_minister = "Breitscheid"; interior_minister_party = "PSOE"; interior_minister = "Severing"; justice_minister_party = "PSOE"; justice_minister = "Radbruch"; labor_minister_party = "PSOE"; labor_minister = "Wissell"; reichswehr_minister_party = "PSOE"; reichswehr_minister = "Leber"; economic_minister_party = "PSOE"; economic_minister = "Schmidt"; finance_minister_party = "PSOE"; finance_minister = "Hilferding"; agriculture_minister_party = "PSOE"; agriculture_minister = "Baade"; public_instruction_minister_party = "PSOE"; public_instruction_minister = "Fernando de los Ríos"; public_works_minister_party = "PSOE"; public_works_minister = "Indalecio Prieto"; ejercito_loyalty -= 0.1; 

We have appointed Indalecio Prieto as president of the Council of Ministers.

- @far_right_coup
- @emergency_no_confidence


@bruning_emergency_chancellor
on-arrival: chancellor = "Martinez Barrios"; chancellor_party = "UR"; psoe_in_government = 1; in_psoe_majority = 1; pro_republic += 5; foreign_minister_party = "PSOE"; foreign_minister = "Breitscheid"; interior_minister_party = "PSOE"; interior_minister = "Severing"; justice_minister_party = "PSOE"; justice_minister = "Radbruch"; labor_minister_party = "PSOE"; labor_minister = "Wissell"; reichswehr_minister_party = "PSOE"; reichswehr_minister = "Leber"; economic_minister_party = "PSOE"; economic_minister = "Schmidt"; finance_minister_party = "PSOE"; finance_minister = "Hilferding"; agriculture_minister_party = "PSOE"; agriculture_minister = "Baade"; public_instruction_minister_party = "PSOE"; public_instruction_minister = "Fernando de los Ríos"; public_works_minister_party = "PSOE"; public_works_minister = "Indalecio Prieto"; ejercito_loyalty -= 0.1; 

The Union Republicana is pleased, and somewhat surprised, that we have appointed [+ chancellor +] as president of the Council of Ministers.

- @far_right_coup
- @emergency_no_confidence

@wirth_emergency_chancellor
view-if: president != "Azana"
on-arrival: chancellor = "Azana"; chancellor_party = ar_name; psoe_in_government = 1; in_psoe_majority = 1; pro_republic += 5; foreign_minister_party = "PSOE"; foreign_minister = "Breitscheid"; interior_minister_party = "PSOE"; interior_minister = "Severing"; justice_minister_party = "PSOE"; justice_minister = "Radbruch"; labor_minister_party = "PSOE"; labor_minister = "Wissell"; reichswehr_minister_party = "PSOE"; reichswehr_minister = "Leber"; economic_minister_party = "PSOE"; economic_minister = "Schmidt"; finance_minister_party = "PSOE"; finance_minister = "Hilferding"; agriculture_minister_party = "PSOE"; agriculture_minister = "Baade"; public_instruction_minister_party = "PSOE"; public_instruction_minister = "Fernando de los Ríos"; public_works_minister_party = "PSOE"; public_works_minister = "Indalecio Prieto"; ejercito_loyalty -= 0.1; 

The Izquierda Republicana is pleased that we have appointed [+ chancellor +] as president of the Council of Ministers.

- @far_right_coup
- @emergency_no_confidence



@far_right_coup
title: The conservative and reactionary parties immediately launch a military coup against us...
view-if: far_right_coalition >= 45
on-arrival: mf_strength += 150; rc_strength += 150; mf_militancy += 0.05; rc_militancy += 0.05

The far-right parties, seeing that we are willing to deny them government by questionably democratic means, have decided that they can only take power by undemocratic means, and have risen up in force against the sitting government.

Their numbers are bolstered by the many government workers who are against the prospect of a unified Socialist government. Police and soldiers defect to the Requetes and Milicias Falangistas.

- @civil_war: It is war.


@emergency_no_confidence
title: The CEDA immediately call a no-confidence vote against us...
view-if: far_right_coalition < 45
on-arrival: prr_no_confidence = 1 if prr_relation < 45; prrs_no_confidence = 1 if prrs_relation < 45; regionalists_no_confidence = 1 if regionalists_relation < 45; dlr_no_confidence = 1 if dlr_relation < 45; ur_no_confidence = 1 if ur_relation < 45; other_no_confidence = 1 if (other_left_republicans_relation + other_right_republicans_relation)/2 < 45; ar_no_confidence = 1 if ar_relation < 45; mf_strength += 200; pce_no_confidence = 1 if pce_relation < 45; rc_strength += 70; no_confidence_votes = ap_r + agrarios_r + re_r + jons_r; no_confidence_votes += prr_r if prr_no_confidence; no_confidence_votes += prrs_r if prrs_no_confidence; no_confidence_votes += pce_r if pce_no_confidence; no_confidence_votes += ar_r if ar_no_confidence; no_confidence_votes += dlr_r if dlr_no_confidence; no_confidence_votes += ur_r if ur_no_confidence; no_confidence_votes += regionalists_r if regionalists_no_confidence; no_confidence_votes += other_left_republicans_r if other_no_confidence; no_confidence_votes += other_right_republicans_r if other_no_confidence; no_confidence_succeeds = 1 if no_confidence_votes > 50

CAMBIAR EL TEXTO ESTE The CEDA, RE and agrarians will vote against us, of course. The other parties vote their conscience. [? if z_no_confidence: The Center Party is voting against us. ?] [? if kpd_no_confidence: The KPD votes against us. ?] [? if other_no_confidence: The assortment of minor parties are voting against us. ?]

In total, [+ no_confidence_votes +]% of the Cortes is against us. [? if no_confidence_succeeds : We have lost the vote of no confidence. ?]

- @no_confidence_elections_new: There will be new elections, which we will try to delay. CAMBIAR EFECTOS
- @no_confidence_win: We have won, for now.


@no_confidence_elections_new
on-arrival: {!
Q.in_emergency_government = 1;
Q.no_majority_elections += 1;
Q.next_election_month = Q.month + 6;
Q.next_election_time = Q.time + 6;
if (Q.next_election_month > 12) {
    Q.next_election_month -= 12;
    Q.next_election_year = Q.year + 1;
} else {
    Q.next_election_year = Q.year;
}
Q.pro_republic -= 5;
Q.workers_spd -= 3;
Q.new_middle_spd -= 3;
Q.old_middle_spd -= 3;
Q.rural_spd -= 3;
Q.catholics_spd -= 3;
Q.workers_nsdap += 5;
Q.old_middle_nsdap += 3;
Q.new_middle_nsdap += 3;
Q.rural_nsdap += 3;
Q.unemployed_nsdap += 5;
if (Q.pro_republic < 45 && Q.pro_republic >= 38) {
    Q.workers_spd -= 6;
}
if (Q.pro_republic < 38) {
    Q.workers_spd *= 0.85;
    Q.new_middle_spd -= 5;
    Q.old_middle_spd -= 5;
    Q.rural_spd -= 5;
    Q.catholics_spd -= 3;
    Q.workers_nsdap += 5;
    Q.old_middle_nsdap += 5;
    Q.new_middle_nsdap += 5;
    Q.rural_nsdap += 5;
    Q.unemployed_nsdap += 5;   
}
!}
view-if: no_confidence_votes > 50

The next elections are set for [+ next_election_month : month +] [+ next_election_year +].


@no_confidence_win
view-if: no_confidence_votes <= 50
on-arrival: in_minority_government = 1; in_emergency_government = 0;
achievement: minderheitsregierung

We have won the vote of no confidence, and are currently ruling under a PSOE minority government. Now our task is to fix the country.


@weimar_coalition
title: We can form a Weimar Coalition.
subtitle: SPD + Z + [+ ddp_name +] [? if sapd_formed and kpd_relation >= 30 : + SAPD toleration ?] ([+ weimar_coalition +]%)
view-if: weimar_coalition >= 50
on-arrival: leverage += 5; leverage += 5 if z_party_leader == "Joos"; in_weimar_coalition = 1; spd_in_government = 1; in_popular_front = 0; in_left_front = 0; foreign_minister_party = "Z"; interior_minister_party = "Z"; justice_minister_party = ddp_name; labor_minister_party = "Z"; reichswehr_minister_party = "I"; economic_minister_party = ddp_name; finance_minister_party = "Z"; agriculture_minister_party = "Z"; foreign_minister = "Wirth"; interior_minister = "Wirth"; justice_minister = "Koch-Weser"; labor_minister = "Stegerwald"; reichswehr_minister = "Groener"; economic_minister = "Dietrich"; finance_minister = "Köhler"; agriculture_minister = "Hermes";
achievement: weimar_coalition

We have enough votes to form a "Weimar Coalition" government consisting of the SPD, Center (Z) and Democratic ([+ ddp_name +]) parties! This has been our preferred governing coalition since 1919.

Who should be the chancellor?

- @muller
- @braun
- @breitscheid_coalition_chancellor
- @wels
- @z_chancellor
- @z_chancellor_wirth

@breitscheid_coalition_chancellor
title: Rudolf Breitscheid for Chancellor
subtitle: Breitscheid is viewed as friendlier towards the left of the SPD.
view-if: year >= 1930
on-arrival: chancellor = "Breitscheid"; chancellor_party = "SPD";
